From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:54:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(llama-cpp): a full card fails the request inside an op
 too, instead of ending the process

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0028-sycl-op-refusal-fails-the-graph.patch), after 0016/0018,
whose pool refusal it extends to the rest of an op.

A node, 2026-11-27: a speech request on a card at 30.7 of 32 GB ended
the backend with "level_zero backend failed with error: 39
(UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY)" caught by a matrix product's
handler, exit 1. Within a graph, a refusal of device memory met by an op -
a kernel's launch, a copy, oneMKL's own workspace - now fails the graph as
the pool's refusal does (GGML_STATUS_ALLOC_FAILED): the request fails, the
process and every model in it stay. Any other exception, and any outside a
graph, ends the process as before. GGML_SYCL_OP_REFUSE=N (armed by
GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_REFUSE_ARM's file) raises the node's error for a test.

Checked: a standalone test of 7 cases; the SYCL backend compiles with
icpx. Not run on a card.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
---
 ...0028-sycl-op-refusal-fails-the-graph.patch | 697 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 697 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0028-sycl-op-refusal-fails-the-graph.patch

diff --git a/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0028-sycl-op-refusal-fails-the-graph.patch b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0028-sycl-op-refusal-fails-the-graph.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e70a8a1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0028-sycl-op-refusal-fails-the-graph.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,697 @@
+ggml-sycl: a refusal of device memory met inside an op fails the graph, as the pool's does, instead of ending the process
+
+On a card shared with other models a full device is contention: the pool's
+refusal already fails the graph (GGML_STATUS_ALLOC_FAILED) and the process
+goes on. A refusal met anywhere else in an op did not: a kernel's launch, a
+copy or a library call (oneMKL allocates its own workspace) raises a
+sycl::exception, and the op's handler ended the process - its
+function-try-block with std::exit(1), or CHECK_TRY_ERROR around one call
+with an abort. A node, 2026-11-27: a speech request on a card at 30.7 of
+32 GB, "level_zero backend failed with error: 39
+(UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY)Exception caught at file:...
+ggml-sycl.cpp, line:3828" (ggml_sycl_op_mul_mat_sycl), exit 1, and LocalAI
+loaded the model again.
+
+The rule (op-refusal.hpp): WITHIN A GRAPH (a flag set while
+ggml_sycl_graph_compute_or_fail() computes one), an exception that says
+the device had no memory - errc::memory_allocation, or the runtime's words
+for it, which come with errc::runtime and the cause in the message alone -
+is thrown on as the pool's refusal (ggml_sycl_out_of_device_memory, moved to
+common.hpp) and fails the graph. Anything else, and anything outside a
+graph (a load, a copy of weights, a SYCL graph's recording), ends the
+process exactly as before: a device that FAILS is no request's to survive.
+The 37 op handlers of ggml-sycl.cpp and mmq.cpp ask it
+(ggml_sycl_op_exception()), and CHECK_TRY_ERROR asks it first
+(ggml_sycl_refusal_from()).
+
+GGML_SYCL_OP_REFUSE=N, armed by GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_REFUSE_ARM's file, makes the
+next N matrix products raise the node's error 39 as the runtime raised it,
+for a test on the card. Without it: one comparison.
+
+Checked: tests/test-sycl-op-refusal.cpp, standard library only, 7 cases
+(the node's words within a graph and outside, errc::memory_allocation, the
+host's memory, a device lost, no words, an older runtime's words); the SYCL
+backend compiles with icpx (oneAPI 2025.3). Not run on a card.
